      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the pro side, argue that nuclear deterrence, through the \"balance of terror,\" directly prevents large-scale conventional war between major powers, making it a necessary, albeit terrible, evil for global stability. This \"deterrence stability\" argument posits that the certainty of mutual assured destruction (MAD) is a better outcome for the world than the guaranteed catastrophic conflict that would follow the breakdown of that balance.\n\nFor the opposition, a weak argument to counter is simply \"nuclear weapons are inherently immoral because they cause mass death and are a constant threat to all human life in the world right now.\" This is easy to attack because it is absolute and fails to address the political and strategic * function* of the weapon in the real world of great power politics.",
